<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Poison Ivy</h1>
<p>Sphere: Poison Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 9)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast poison ivy &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>The caster touches the target and growls 'Rasica Potio', and their skin 
breaks out in an ugly red rash. Every half minute the rash torments 
them: first an itch, then painful blisters, then several rounds of 
scratching it bloody, each costing them 13 to 17 hit points, and at last 
it subsides and heals. The better the casting, the more rounds of 
scratching. Someone who already has the rash can't catch it again.
</p><p>The target resists with their mind, and casting it is an attack: they 
will fight you for it. A strong enough <a cmd='#'>Help Remove Disease</a> heals the 
rash at once; remove poison does not. You must be standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Remove Disease</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Poison Sphere</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Druid Spells</a>
</pre>




</div>